                <pb facs="0172" n="74" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg74"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">850d.00/361a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Commission to Negotiate
                            Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-04-05T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 5, 1919—4
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>1458. For Secretary Lansing from Phillips.</p>
                <p>Norwegian Minister called this morning under instructions from his Government to
                    request that the Government of the United States lend its support to the
                    representations which the Norwegian representatives in Paris are now making
                    regarding Spitzbergen, which Norway desires to have recognized as Norwegian
                    territory. I assured the Minister that I would not fail to communicate his
                    request to you.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
